# Statutory-value CI protection, per ADR-0005.
#
# GitHub auto-requests review from the listed owner on any PR touching these
# paths. On the current plan this is a soft signal, not a hard merge block —
# branch protection ("require review from Code Owners") needs GitHub Pro for
# a private repo, which this repo doesn't have yet. See ADR-0005 and
# .github/workflows/statutory-value-guard.yml for the rest of the mechanism.
#
# Whole files are the enforced boundary (CODEOWNERS can't target a YAML
# sub-section); for policy.yaml, the parameters block is *why* it's
# protected, not the scope — non-statutory edits are also gated as an
# accepted coarseness cost.

policy_specs/working_for_families/benchmarks.yaml    @hemmingsenpeter-byte
policy_specs/working_for_families/spec_cases.yaml    @hemmingsenpeter-byte
policy_specs/working_for_families/policy.yaml        @hemmingsenpeter-byte
